  "narrative": {
    "intro": "SK Energy obligated $329M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. SK Energy has won 25 awards so far this fiscal year, at an average award size of $13.1M. SK Energy's obligations are up 136.0% year over year. SK Energy's fiscal-year obligations climbed steadily from FY21 through FY25: $28.2M in FY21, $37.3M in FY22, $64.3M in FY23, $80.8M in FY24, and $139M in FY25. SK Energy's FY26 total of $329M reflects a material step up relative to prior years. SK Energy's current-year totals are partial, covering fiscal year to date, and the note clarifies that figures are contract obligations except where award-value figures are called out in other tables. This snapshot highlights scale and recent growth in SK Energy's federal business, showing concentration of new obligations in FY26 and a pattern of expanding annual obligations since FY21.",
